{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_backoff_policy_backoffpolicy", "label": "BackoffPolicy", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A function from how many times this failed to how long to wait, decoupled from any supervisor or retry loop so the calculation is trivially testable and reusable. restartCount is 0-based and the delay is in milliseconds.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_backoff_policy_exponentialbackoff", "label": "exponentialBackoff", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "min times 2^n clamped to max, then jittered. Exponential is the better choice for recovery because a failing upstream needs time to heal, and clamping prevents pathologically long waits after many failures.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_backoff_policy_linearbackoff", "label": "linearBackoff", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "min plus step times n clamped to max, same jitter contract. Niche: a polling cadence that should level off quickly, or a producer rate-limiting itself so the growth in wait matches steady-state acceptable load.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_backoff_policy_jitter", "label": "Jitter and the thundering herd", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "When N clients retry at the same delay they synchronize their next attempt, raising the chance the upstream stays broken; plus or minus 20 percent noise scatters retries so the herd disperses. Values beyond 1.0 are rejected.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_backoff_policy_injectable_random", "label": "Injectable random for determinism", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Both policies accept a random override so delayFor is reproducible in tests; a linear congruential generator is good enough there and Math.random is fine in production.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_backoff_policy_retry_budget", "label": "Pair backoff with a retry budget", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The policy clamps cleanly at max, but a caller waiting five minutes between attempts has gone past transient failure into dead upstream; cap total attempts or elapsed time and surface a permanent failure to an alert.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_backoff_policy_custom_policy", "label": "Custom backoff policies", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Implementing the one-method interface - a fibonacci policy, for instance - and passing it as the policy option overrides the default exponential growth.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_backoff_policy_exponentialbackoff", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_backoff_policy_backoffpolicy", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/backoff-policy.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"so